[4] Structural readout
    The strong AP-extremal conjecture is false as stated: k=12 and k=13
    have near-AP tail shapes that beat the plain AP.  This is useful,
    because those rows have enormous cap slack; the dangerous margins are
    k=8..11, where widened primitive boxes found no AP-beater.
    The corrected route is an AP-frontier envelope: prove AP extremal for
    k=8..11, and prove a coarse AP-rich envelope for k=12,13.  High-spread
    dissociated/Sidon/quadratic rows fall far below either envelope.

